<section class="rs-s rs-qt" id="qty"><div class="rs-w rs-qt-g"><div><p class="rs-ey">Tool one</p><h2 class="rv">Risotto quantity calculator</h2><p class="rs-p">Tell us how many are coming and how you are serving it. We scale the rice, stock and finishing ingredients so nobody goes hungry and nothing is wasted.</p>
<label class="rs-lb" for="qt-g">Guests <output id="qt-go">4</output></label><input type="range" id="qt-g" min="1" max="12" value="4">
<fieldset><legend>Served as</legend><div class="rs-chips" id="qt-c"><button type="button" data-v="0">A starter</button><button type="button" data-v="1" class="on">The main course</button></div></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Style</legend><div class="rs-chips" id="qt-s"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on">Parmesan</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Mushroom</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Saffron</button><button type="button" data-v="3">Spring vegetable</button></div></fieldset><figure class="rs-qt-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1613758235256-43a7bdc21d82?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&h=260&q=75" alt="a close-up of uncooked arborio rice" width="600" height="260" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div class="rs-card"><p class="rs-card-k">La spesa</p><h3>Your shopping list</h3><ul class="rs-list" id="qt-l" aria-live="polite"></ul><p class="rs-small" id="qt-n"></p></div></div></section>

<section class="rs-s rs-tm" id="timer"><div class="rs-w rs-tm-g"><div class="rs-tm-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 300" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="150" cy="150" r="130" class="trk"/><circle id="tm-ring" cx="150" cy="150" r="130" class="ring"/><circle cx="150" cy="150" r="104" class="pan"/><circle cx="150" cy="150" r="92" class="rice" id="tm-rice"/></svg><div class="rs-tm-c"><b id="tm-t">0:00</b><span id="tm-s">Ready</span></div></div>
<div><p class="rs-ey">Tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Stirring timer</h2><p class="rs-p">Risotto rewards attention. Start the timer as the rice goes in and we will tell you when to add stock, when to taste and when to finish. Try practice mode to run through the whole process in under a minute.</p>
<div class="rs-tm-b"><button type="button" class="rs-btn rs-btn2" id="tm-go">Start cooking</button><button type="button" class="rs-ghost" id="tm-r">Reset</button><label class="rs-ck"><input type="checkbox" id="tm-f" checked> Practice mode (1 minute = 2 seconds)</label></div>
<ol class="rs-steps" id="tm-l"><li data-t="0"><b>0:00</b>Toast the rice in the hot fat until glassy.</li><li data-t="2"><b>2:00</b>Add the first ladle of hot stock and stir.</li><li data-t="4"><b>4 to 14</b>Add a ladle each time the last is nearly absorbed.</li><li data-t="15"><b>15:00</b>Taste: the grain should be tender with a little bite.</li><li data-t="18"><b>18:00</b>Off the heat. Beat in cold butter and cheese.</li><li data-t="20"><b>20:00</b>Rest for two minutes, then serve in warm bowls.</li></ol><p class="rs-ladles" aria-live="polite">Ladles added: <b id="tm-ld">0</b></p><figure class="rs-tm-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1584450086321-06632ca7faa7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&h=260&q=75" alt="freshly grated parmesan beside a grater" width="600" height="260" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="rs-s rs-st"><div class="rs-w"><div class="rs-sh rs-sh-c"><p class="rs-ey">Il metodo</p><h2 class="rv">Four stages, one rhythm</h2></div><ol class="rs-stages stg"><li class="rv"><div class="rs-stg-i"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="46" fill="#F3E2B8"/><g fill="#FFF8E6" stroke="#D9C089"><path d="M22 30q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M37 30q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M52 30q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M67 30q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M22 46q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M37 46q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M52 46q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M67 46q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M22 62q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M37 62q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M52 62q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/><path d="M67 62q6-8 12 0q-6 8-12 0z"/></g></svg></div><span>01</span><b>Soffritto</b><em>Soften</em><p>Onion or shallot cooks gently in butter or olive oil until sweet and translucent, never brown.</p></li><li class="rv"><div class="rs-stg-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1706345624391-6885ae0c4aad?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="small mushrooms growing on a forest floor" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></div><span>02</span><b>Tostatura</b><em>Toast</em><p>The rice is stirred in the hot fat for a minute or two until the grains turn glassy at the edges.</p></li><li class="rv"><div class="rs-stg-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1656568866961-03e9dcc0fbc6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="red saffron threads" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></div><span>03</span><b>Cottura</b><em>Simmer</em><p>Hot stock goes in a ladle at a time. Each addition is stirred until almost absorbed, for about 18 minutes.</p></li><li class="rv"><div class="rs-stg-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1683314573422-649a3c6ad784?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="wedges of hard cheese on a board" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></div><span>04</span><b>Mantecatura</b><em>Finish</em><p>Off the heat, cold butter and grated cheese are beaten in until the risotto flows like a slow wave.</p></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="rs-s rs-mn"><div class="rs-w rs-mn-g"><div class="rs-menu rv"><p class="rs-menu-k">Menu della sera</p><h2>A risotto dinner</h2><ul><li><div><b>Antipasto</b><i></i><em>Something light to start</em></div><p>A simple salad of leaves, fennel and citrus, or grilled vegetables with olive oil.</p></li><li><div><b>Primo</b><i></i><em>The risotto</em></div><p>Served straight from the pan in warm, shallow bowls, all'onda: flowing, never stiff.</p></li><li><div><b>Secondo</b><i></i><em>Optional</em></div><p>If guests are hungry, a little roast fish or chicken with greens; risotto is often filling enough.</p></li><li><div><b>Dolce</b><i></i><em>To finish</em></div><p>Fresh fruit, a lemon tart or a scoop of gelato keeps the end of the meal light.</p></li></ul><p class="rs-menu-f">Serve the risotto the moment it is ready; it waits for no one.</p></div><div class="rs-mn-v"><figure class="rs-mn-i pxw"><img data-px=".08" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1662114757324-fb95be6dceaf?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=400&q=75" alt="a plate of risotto on a set dinner table" width="560" height="400" loading="lazy"></figure><div class="rs-gal"><figure class="rs-pl rv"><div class="rs-pl-r"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1767065584562-0127cdec486d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=480&h=480&q=75" alt="risotto served in a wide white bowl" width="480" height="480" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Classico</figcaption></figure><figure class="rs-pl rv"><div class="rs-pl-r"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633964913295-ceb43826e7c9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=480&h=480&q=75" alt="risotto in a deep bowl with a spoon" width="480" height="480" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Cremoso</figcaption></figure></div></div></div></section>

